course: dictionary
lesson: 12209
title: Congregating
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Congregating means gathering together in a group or crowd in one place. It is the -ing form of congregate, so it describes something happening right now: «Hundreds of zebras were congregating at the waterhole.» The clues are hundreds and waterhole, so many animals are coming together in one spot.
explain: Look at the words around it: «Children were congregating outside the school gates before the bell.» Outside the gates and before the bell tell you the children are gathering in a crowd and waiting. Check by putting your meaning in the sentence: gathering together fits, so you know you are right.
explain: Congregating often comes with words like around or outside, as in «congregating around» or «congregating outside». In a church, people who come together to worship are congregating too, and that group is called a congregation. The idea is the same: many people in one place.
fact: Congregating is a verb. It is the -ing form of congregate.
fact: «Congregating» means gathering together in a group or crowd in one place.
fact: In a church, people who are congregating are coming together to worship.
fact: The group of people who worship together in a church is called a «congregation».
fact: A sign reading «No congregating in the corridor» tells people not to gather in a crowd there.
exercise: «Hundreds of zebras were congregating at the waterhole.» What does congregating mean? | Running away quickly | Drinking alone | *Gathering together in a crowd | Sleeping under the trees
exercise: «Children were congregating outside the school gates.» Find and copy the word that shows they were gathering in a group. | school | gates | outside | *congregating
exercise: Complete the rule: «No ___ in the corridor.» Which word fits? | shouting | *congregating | eating | running
test: «Shoppers were congregating around the new bakery.» What does congregating mean here? | Walking slowly past | Being very quiet | *Coming together in a crowd | Closing the shop early
test: What do we call the group of people who come together to worship in a church? | *Congregation | Choir | Team | Audience
exam: Which word means gathering together in a group in one place? | Vanishing | Wandering | Scattering | *Congregating
